Subject: Defer Rime notifications outside engine mutation

librime invokes its notification handler synchronously from ProcessKey and
SetOption while the engine graph is still mutating.  Entering AppKit from that
callback can synchronously re-enter InputMethodKit and start another Rime key
operation on the same stack.  Copy the callback's transient C strings and
defer every UI or Rime action to the next main-run-loop turn.  Drop option
notifications whose pointer-derived session ID is no longer live.

